---
import BaseHead from '../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';

const description =
	'Diagram Loom — a Tauri desktop app that manages deployment and connectivity data for a system, lints it for gaps, and produces C4 Model diagrams.';

const stack = [
	'Rust',
	'Tauri',
	'Vue 3 + TypeScript',
	'maxGraph',
	'elkjs',
	'tauri-specta',
	'serde / YAML',
	'calamine (xlsx)',
	'MCP',
	'Playwright / WebdriverIO',
];
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title="Diagram Loom" description={description} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<div class="lang-switch" role="group" aria-label="Language">
				<button type="button" data-lang-btn="zh" class="active">中文</button>
				<button type="button" data-lang-btn="en">EN</button>
			</div>

			<!-- 中文 -->
			<section data-lang="zh" lang="zh-Hant">
				<h1>Diagram Loom</h1>
				<p class="tagline">
					一套桌面應用程式，管理系統的部署與連線資訊，檢查有沒有漏掉的連線，並產出 C4 Model 圖。
				</p>

				<h2>專案簡介</h2>
				<p>
					畫架構圖的工具已經很多了，但真正的痛點不在畫圖：當一套系統有數百條連線時，怕的是<strong>漏掉其中一條</strong>。所以
					Diagram Loom 的核心不是畫布，而是<strong>連線的完整性管理與 Linting</strong>——圖只是這份資料的其中一種呈現方式。
				</p>
				<p>
					它刻意不做 code → diagram 的逆向工程，也不掃描真實環境做自動發現。資料由人維護，工具負責在存檔時告訴你「這個環境還缺什麼」。
				</p>

				<h2>核心概念：兩層模型</h2>
				<p>
					<strong>邏輯層是母版，環境層是分身。</strong>邏輯層定義「有哪些服務、誰要連誰」（<code>Container</code>、<code>Relationship</code>）；環境層填「實際跑在哪台機器、IP
					是什麼、幾個節點」（<code>ContainerInstance</code>、<code>Connection</code>）。
				</p>
				<p>
					通則只有一條：<strong>邏輯層有的東西，每個環境都必須實現，沒實現就 lint
					報錯</strong>。命名全面對齊 C4——這裡的 <code>Container</code> 是服務（Redis、Consul），機器叫
					<code>Deployment Node</code>，F5 這類 VIP 設備叫 <code>Infrastructure Node</code>。
				</p>

				<h2>架構亮點</h2>
				<ul>
					<li>
						<strong>規則在 Rust，畫面與檔案格式在 JavaScript</strong> —— 領域模型、lint、Excel 匯入、三方對帳的判斷都在
						Rust；Vue 負責畫面、畫布與 <code>.drawio</code> 讀寫。判斷標準是「這是<em>規則</em>還是<em>轉接</em>」。
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Hexagonal，但只畫該畫的那條線</strong> —— <code>loom-core</code> 不相依
						<code>tauri</code>，核心不知道自己被誰呼叫，因此大部分邏輯都能用 <code>cargo test</code>
						驗證。這條紀律由一個 CI 檢查守著。
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>自己的 maxGraph 畫布</strong> —— 一開始是內嵌 draw.io 的
						iframe，實測後換成自己跑 maxGraph：同一個文件、同一套事件，不再隔著
						postMessage。<code>.drawio</code> 留下來當檔案格式，讀寫兩邊都自己寫。
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>自動排版</strong> —— elkjs，只用 <code>layered</code>；實測下來只有它處理得了巢狀容器加上跨容器的邊。2480
						個節點排版約 6 秒，數百節點不到 1 秒。
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>三方對帳</strong> —— 圖是人手改過的，模型也會變。存檔時比對「圖／模型／上次的 base
						快照」三方，逐項判斷哪邊動了。JS 說「圖上有什麼」，Rust 說「這代表什麼」。
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>給 AI Agent 的 MCP 端點</strong> —— 八支工具、三種形狀（讀 <code>{'{scope, select, detail}'}</code>、寫
						<code>{'{scope, items, dry_run}'}</code>、刪 <code>{'{scope, targets, cascade, confirm}'}</code>），讓 Agent
						不必把整份專案倒出來就能問「prod 的 redis 建好了沒」。
					</li>
				</ul>

				<h2>Lint：這個專案的靈魂</h2>
				<p>
					目前 14 條規則（L001–L014），分 Error / Warning / Info 三級。幾條代表性的：
				</p>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>L001</strong> —— 邏輯層元素在某環境沒有任何實現。</li>
					<li><strong>L002</strong> —— 某條連線在某環境<strong>走不通</strong>（可達性斷裂，例如 F5 設了但後面沒接）。用 BFS 檢查。</li>
					<li><strong>L004 / L005</strong> —— 萬用字元的實際數量與 <code>expect</code> 不符，或根本沒註明 <code>expect</code>。</li>
					<li><strong>L006</strong> —— Endpoint 缺少實際位址（IP / port / URL / 路徑）。</li>
					<li><strong>L013</strong> —— 契約的目標端是人。人只能當來源，他沒有接點也不會被部署。</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					每一條會叫的 lint，面板上都要有對應的操作能就地修好——這是刻意的要求，不是加分項。
				</p>

				<h2>資料怎麼存</h2>
				<p>
					一個 Project 就是<strong>一個資料夾</strong>，內含多個 YAML 檔：<code>logical/</code>
					放邏輯層，<code>environments/</code> 一個環境一個檔，<code>diagrams/</code>
					放圖。全部是純文字，可以進版控、可以 diff、可以 code review。元素用 UUID 當身分證、slug 當顯示名。
				</p>

				<h2>技術棧</h2>
				<div class="tags">
					{stack.map((item) => <span class="tag">{item}</span>)}
				</div>

				<h2>開發狀態</h2>
				<p>
					主動開發中。領域模型、lint、Excel 匯入、表格與 lint 面板、編輯與復原、資源
					CRUD、MCP 端點、圖的節點／連線／篩選／標註／存檔都已完成。下一步是<strong>對帳面板的
					UI</strong>——三方比對的判斷已經在 Rust 做完了，缺的是讓人逐項裁決差異的那個畫面，也是這個專案最難的一塊。
				</p>

				<h2>連結</h2>
				<ul>
					<li>
						<a href="https://github.com/lanyitin/diagram-loom">github.com/lanyitin/diagram-loom</a>
						—— 原始碼：Rust 的 <code>loom-core</code> 與 <code>loom-mcp</code>、Tauri 殼、Vue
						前端。設計文件與決策紀錄目前還放在本機的 workspace 裡，尚未公開。
					</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<!-- English -->
			<section data-lang="en" lang="en" hidden>
				<h1>Diagram Loom</h1>
				<p class="tagline">
					A desktop app that manages a system's deployment and connectivity data, lints it for
					missing links, and produces C4 Model diagrams.
				</p>

				<h2>Overview</h2>
				<p>
					There is no shortage of diagramming tools, but the real pain isn't drawing: when a system
					has hundreds of connections, what you fear is <strong>missing one of them</strong>. So the
					core of Diagram Loom isn't the canvas — it's <strong>completeness management and linting
					over the connections</strong>. Diagrams are just one way to render that data.
				</p>
				<p>
					It deliberately does not reverse-engineer code into diagrams, and it does not scan live
					environments for discovery. People maintain the data; the tool's job is to tell you, on
					save, what this environment is still missing.
				</p>

				<h2>The Core Idea: Two Layers</h2>
				<p>
					<strong>The logical layer is the master; each environment is a copy of it.</strong> The
					logical layer declares what services exist and who must talk to whom
					(<code>Container</code>, <code>Relationship</code>); the environment layer fills in which
					machine it actually runs on, what the IP is, and how many nodes there are
					(<code>ContainerInstance</code>, <code>Connection</code>).
				</p>
				<p>
					There is exactly one rule: <strong>everything in the logical layer must be realized in
					every environment, or lint reports it</strong>. Naming follows C4 throughout — a
					<code>Container</code> here is a service (Redis, Consul), machines are
					<code>Deployment Node</code>s, and VIP appliances like F5 are
					<code>Infrastructure Node</code>s.
				</p>

				<h2>Architecture</h2>
				<ul>
					<li>
						<strong>Rules in Rust, views and file formats in JavaScript</strong> — the domain model,
						lint, Excel import, and the three-way reconciliation verdict all live in Rust; Vue owns
						the UI, the canvas, and <code>.drawio</code> read/write. The test is whether something is
						a <em>rule</em> or an <em>adapter</em>.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Hexagonal, but only where it earns its keep</strong> — <code>loom-core</code> does
						not depend on <code>tauri</code>; the core doesn't know who calls it, so most of the
						logic is verifiable with plain <code>cargo test</code>. A CI check guards that boundary.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Our own maxGraph canvas</strong> — it started as an embedded draw.io iframe, then
						moved to running maxGraph directly: one document, one event system, no postMessage in
						between. <code>.drawio</code> stays as the file format, with both sides hand-written.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Automatic layout</strong> — elkjs, <code>layered</code> only; in testing it was
						the only algorithm that handled nested containers plus edges crossing them. 2,480 nodes
						lay out in about 6 seconds; a few hundred take under a second.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Three-way reconciliation</strong> — diagrams get edited by hand and the model
						moves too. On save, the diagram, the model, and the previous base snapshot are compared
						so each difference can be adjudicated. JS says <em>what's on the diagram</em>; Rust says
						<em>what that means</em>.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>An MCP surface for AI agents</strong> — eight tools in three shapes (read
						<code>{'{scope, select, detail}'}</code>, write <code>{'{scope, items, dry_run}'}</code>,
						delete <code>{'{scope, targets, cascade, confirm}'}</code>), so an agent can ask "is redis
						set up in prod yet?" without dumping the whole project first.
					</li>
				</ul>

				<h2>Lint: The Heart of It</h2>
				<p>
					Fourteen rules today (L001–L014) across Error / Warning / Info. A representative few:
				</p>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>L001</strong> — a logical element is not realized at all in some environment.</li>
					<li>
						<strong>L002</strong> — a relationship is <strong>unreachable</strong> in some environment
						(e.g. the F5 is configured but nothing sits behind it). Checked with BFS.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>L004 / L005</strong> — a wildcard's actual count doesn't match its
						<code>expect</code>, or has no <code>expect</code> at all.
					</li>
					<li><strong>L006</strong> — an endpoint has no concrete address (IP / port / URL / path).</li>
					<li>
						<strong>L013</strong> — a contract targets a person. People can only be a source; they
						have no endpoints and don't get deployed.
					</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					Every lint that can fire must have a corresponding fix in the panel — that's a requirement,
					not a nice-to-have.
				</p>

				<h2>Storage</h2>
				<p>
					A project is <strong>a folder</strong> of YAML files: <code>logical/</code> for the logical
					layer, <code>environments/</code> with one file per environment, <code>diagrams/</code> for
					the diagrams. All plain text — versionable, diffable, reviewable. Elements carry a UUID as
					identity and a slug as display name.
				</p>

				<h2>Tech Stack</h2>
				<div class="tags">
					{stack.map((item) => <span class="tag">{item}</span>)}
				</div>

				<h2>Status</h2>
				<p>
					Under active development. The domain model, lint, Excel import, the table and lint panels,
					editing and undo, resource CRUD, the MCP endpoints, and the diagram work (nodes, edges,
					filtering, annotation, saving) are all done. Next up is <strong>the reconciliation panel
					UI</strong> — the three-way comparison already works in Rust; what's missing is the screen
					where a human adjudicates each difference, and it's the hardest part of the project.
				</p>

				<h2>Links</h2>
				<ul>
					<li>
						<a href="https://github.com/lanyitin/diagram-loom">github.com/lanyitin/diagram-loom</a>
						— the source: the <code>loom-core</code> and <code>loom-mcp</code> Rust crates, the
						Tauri shell, and the Vue front end. The design docs and decision records still live in
						a local workspace and aren't public yet.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</section>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	.lang-switch {
		display: flex;
		gap: 0.25rem;
		justify-content: flex-end;
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
	}
	.lang-switch button {
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: 0.7rem;
		letter-spacing: var(--tracking-label);
		text-transform: uppercase;
		padding: 0.3rem 0.8rem;
		border: var(--rule-width) solid var(--color-rule);
		background: transparent;
		color: var(--color-fg-faint);
		border-radius: var(--radius);
		cursor: pointer;
		transition:
			background var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out),
			color var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out),
			border-color var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out);
	}
	.lang-switch button:hover {
		color: var(--color-fg);
		border-color: var(--color-rule-strong);
	}
	.lang-switch button.active {
		background: var(--color-accent);
		border-color: var(--color-accent);
		color: var(--color-accent-fg);
	}
	.tagline {
		font-size: 1.15rem;
		color: var(--color-fg-muted);
		line-height: 1.7;
	}
	.tags {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 0.5rem;
		margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem;
	}
	.tag {
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: 0.7rem;
		letter-spacing: 0.06em;
		padding: 0.25rem 0.6rem;
		border: var(--rule-width) solid var(--color-rule);
		border-radius: var(--radius);
		background: var(--color-bg-subtle);
		color: var(--color-fg-muted);
	}
</style>

<script>
	const buttons = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-lang-btn]');
	const sections = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-lang]');

	function setLang(lang: string) {
		sections.forEach((section) => {
			section.hidden = section.dataset.lang !== lang;
		});
		buttons.forEach((button) => {
			button.classList.toggle('active', button.dataset.langBtn === lang);
		});
	}

	buttons.forEach((button) => {
		button.addEventListener('click', () => setLang(button.dataset.langBtn!));
	});

	// Default to Chinese; English section starts hidden via markup.
	setLang('zh');
</script>
